  "body": "We currently allow AES128-CCM, which isn't a great cipher and isn't in Mozilla's modern suite.\r\n\r\nWe should also get rid of TLS 1.0 and 1.1, since we require ciphers that basically require a TLS 1.2 compatible TLS stack to talk to.",
